LAST_SUCCESS=Workaround (disable @_typeEraser(DebugReplaceableView) on wasm) TRIED & REVERTED: only changed OOB-trap->hang (AnyView also routes through makeDynamicView/DynamicViewContainer), so eraser choice isn't the cause. REAL ROOT localized: TupleView per-element runtime-conformance witness dispatch. TupleView._makeView -> TypeConformance<ViewDescriptor>.visitType (View.swift:201) -> unsafeBitCast(storage,to:(any View.Type).self) packs the swift_conformsToProtocol witness table into an existential metatype -> calls _makeView via that witness -> OOB call_indirect on wasm (wild funcref). Single-view Content works (skips this path); only TupleView hits it.
NOTES=HYPOTHESES for real fix (need Swift-runtime-on-wasm dig): (a) witness from swift_conformsToProtocol may be un-instantiated generic pattern on wasm -> bad entries (try swift_conformsToProtocolCommon / instantiate); (b) existential-metatype layout / funcref repr differs on wasm (witness fn ptrs = table indices); (c) tupleDescription/TupleType element enumeration yields wrong conformances. NEXT: instrument TypeConformance.visitType + tupleDescription to print element type+witness, confirm _makeView-via-witness is the OOB call. Working on wasm: primitive/custom views, @State reactive, Text, conformance(single). probe=Text+@State (working). View.swift reverted clean. Patches: openswiftui-phase1-wip(19 files, committed 00840b32), compute-wasm, oag-fork. ALL builds ANY_ATTRIBUTE_FIX=0.
